# PCB Layout Visualization - ESP32 Water Quality System

## Board Specifications
- Dimensions: 100mm x 80mm
- Layers: 2 (Top and Bottom)
- Copper Weight: 1 oz (35 μm)
- Board Thickness: 1.6mm
- Finish: HASL (Lead-Free) or ENIG

## Component Placement (ASCII Art Representation)

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  ESP32 Water Quality Monitoring PCB - Top Layer (100mm x 80mm)     │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                     │
│  [BNC-J1]  [GPS-U6]      [ESP32-WROOM-32]       [RFM95W-U5]       │
│     pH     ┌──────┐      ┌──────────────┐       ┌────────┐        │
│            │ NEO  │      │              │       │  LoRa  │ [ANT]  │
│            │  6M  │      │    ESP32     │       │ Module │        │
│            └──────┘      │  Main MCU    │       └────────┘        │
│                          └──────────────┘                          │
│                                                                     │
│  [C9]   [U3]       [C5] [C6] [C1-C4]      [U7-MCP3008]            │
│  1000uF 3.3V       Caps  Caps Decoupling   ┌──────────┐           │
│                                             │   ADC    │           │
│  [C10]  [U4]       [D1]                    │  MCP3008 │           │
│  1000uF 5.0V       Diode                   └──────────┘           │
│                                                                     │
│  [L298N - U2]      [R1-R13]    [Q1-Q4]     [J5-MicroSD]           │
│  ┌────────────┐    Resistors   Transistors ┌─────────┐            │
│  │   Motor    │    Arrays      2N2222      │ SD Card │            │
│  │   Driver   │                            │  Slot   │            │
│  └────────────┘                            └─────────┘            │
│                                                                     │
│  [J3]   [D2-D6]    [SW1] [SW2]    [BZ1]    [J2] [J4]              │
│  Motor  LEDs       Reset  Power   Buzzer   Turb Temp              │
│  2-Pin  Status     Button Switch           4Pin 3Pin              │
│                                                                     │
│  [F1]   [BAT1]     [J6]                                            │
│  Fuse   Battery    Screw Terminal                                 │
│  2A     JST-2P     Power In                                        │
│                                                                     │
│  GND Plane (Bottom Layer)                  Power Plane (Mixed)    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Layer Stack-up

```
┌──────────────────┐
│   Top Copper     │ ← Component side, signal routing
├──────────────────┤
│   FR4 Core       │ ← 1.6mm dielectric
├──────────────────┤
│  Bottom Copper   │ ← Ground plane + power routing
└──────────────────┘
```

## Routing Guidelines

### Power Traces
- VCC (7.4V): 2.0mm width minimum
- 5V Rail: 1.5mm width minimum  
- 3.3V Rail: 1.0mm width minimum
- GND: Solid plane on bottom layer

### Signal Traces
- High-speed (SPI, I2C): 0.3mm, length matched
- UART (GPS): 0.4mm
- GPIO: 0.5mm
- Analog (sensor inputs): 0.5mm, keep away from digital

### Clearances
- Trace-to-trace: 0.2mm minimum
- Trace-to-pad: 0.2mm minimum
- Pad-to-pad: 0.3mm minimum
- Copper-to-edge: 0.5mm minimum

## Critical Routing Notes

1. **ESP32 Module**:
   - Place decoupling caps within 5mm
   - Keep antenna area clear (no copper pour)
   - RF traces impedance controlled (50Ω)

2. **LoRa Module**:
   - SPI traces length-matched within 5mm
   - Keep antenna trace away from other signals
   - Ground plane under module

3. **GPS Module**:
   - Keep away from LoRa and ESP32 antennas
   - Dedicated ground plane under module
   - Antenna trace on top layer

4. **ADC (MCP3008)**:
   - Analog ground separate from digital
   - Star grounding at ADC
   - Shielded traces for sensor inputs

5. **Motor Driver**:
   - Wide traces for motor output (2mm+)
   - Flyback diodes close to driver
   - Heat dissipation area on bottom layer

6. **Power Supply**:
   - Large input capacitors near regulators
   - Kelvin sensing for voltage feedback
   - Thermal relief on regulator pads

## Via Specifications
- Pad Diameter: 0.8mm
- Hole Diameter: 0.4mm
- Annular Ring: 0.2mm minimum

## Silkscreen
- Component designators on top
- Pin 1 indicators marked clearly
- Voltage warnings near power connectors
- Test point labels

## Manufacturing Notes
- Board manufactured to IPC Class 2
- Soldermask: Green (or customer choice)
- Silkscreen: White
- Testing: Flying probe or test points
- Panelization: V-score or tab routing

This is a text representation. The actual PNG would show:
- Color-coded layers (red=top, blue=bottom)
- Component outlines and values
- Trace routing in detail
- Ground plane hatching
- Dimension markers
